<span id="A4.F7.2.13.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Classify the text as "Drivelology" or "non-Drivelology."</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.F7.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.F7.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:2.5pt 2.3pt;">
<span id="A4.F7.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:369.9pt;">
<span id="A4.F7.2.14.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Definitions:</span>
<span id="A4.F7.2.14.1.1.2" class="ltx_p">- Drivelology: Logically coherent statements with paradox, layered or hidden meaning, often using humor, irony, or sarcasm. These require emotional or contextual insight to interpret.</span>
<span id="A4.F7.2.14.1.1.3" class="ltx_p">- non-Drivelology: Pure nonsense or straightforward statements without hidden complexity.</span>
</span></td></tr>
